1400 GOSUB 6360:BM$="Vince: You know that guy Susanna met at the restaurant? Gockel? Turns\out he's a painter. I went to his art gallery to check out his work and well... I\don't see how those paintings could bring home the bacon.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1410 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Clark: Why, you an art critic now? Didn't you tell me his paintings sell like\hotcakes the other time?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1420 GOSUB 6360:BM$="Vince: He sells them to rich people, mostly. He's a smooth talker.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1430 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Clark: You said he has a lot of hobbies. Fortune-telling wouldn't happen to\be one of 'em, would it?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1440 GOSUB 6360:BM$="Vince: He has so much time and money to spare that I had to write it all\down, hold on... Ah, there it is. Yeah, turns out he does have some interest in\fortune-telling.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1450 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Clark: That man Susanna met in Paris... Flannel, the CEO of that trading\company? He also enjoys his fortune-telling, apparently.\Then there's Michael, that fortune-teller Susanna and David saw in Rome.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1460 GOSUB 6360:BM$="Vince: Now that you mention it... I've written down `fortune-telling` a lot in\my notebook. It came up in France, Italy, and now Germany.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1470 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Clark: Alright, let's have the London Association of Detectives look into\any links between Susanna and fortune-telling. My gut tells me they'll find\something.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1480 GOSUB 6360:BM$="Vince: What about the client who asked us to investigate Susanna?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1490 GOSUB 6350:BM$="Clark: I'll give 'em a call once we're back in London.\Well, it's 2 am. They have a concert tomorrow, so I doubt they're doing\anything tonight. Let's go.":GOSUB 5100
